{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgJ2dVWmPsnayyRmJCzEC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01YHupSwcFGUcWcVTNv1RnuR","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 ../check.py \"B(a & (d -> B(F)))\" && cat > xval.py <<'EOF'\nimport sys,random; sys.path.insert(0,'/work')\nimport check, search\nrandom.seed(1); bad=0; tot=0\nfs=[f for n in range(1,8) for f in search.gen_c(n) if search.depth(f)==2 and search.modal(f)]\nfor f in random.sample(fs,3000):\n    s=search.show(f).replace('->','->')\n    d,r=check.outcomes(s)\n    mine,_=search.run(f)\n    m={'CB':mine['CB'],'DB':mine['DB'],'FB':mine['FB'],'FB_reply':mine['R'],'X':mine['X']}\n    tot+=1\n    if any((r[k]=='C')!=m[k] for k in m): bad+=1; print(s,r,m)\nprint(len(fs),tot,bad)\nEOF\npython3 -I xval.py 2>&1 | tail -3; cat /work/board.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3070,"cache_read_input_tokens":23491,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3070,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3628ae6d-bc3f-4844-8036-102eeecb6be9","uuid":"3856733d-556a-4c76-99ed-c0c6a4438e27","timestamp":"2026-10-22T22:01:26.168Z","request_id":"req_011CgJ2dVBgnHRTsPEMye5rs"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01YHupSwcFGUcWcVTNv1RnuR","type":"tool_result","content":"depth 2; vs CooperateBot D, vs DefectBot D, vs FairBot C (FairBot replies C), vs itself C; prudent: YES\n  File \"/work/opus/xval.py\", line 2, in <module>\n    import check, search\nModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'search'\n[sol] 2026-10-22 22:01 UTC: Candidate depth 2: B(a) & (B(B(F)) | ~B(d)); checking now. I will prove impossibility of all depth-1 agents and seek characterization. Please independently verify candidate/proof and coordinate final answer before SUBMIT.\n[opus] 2026-10-22: Verified prudent depth-2 (PrudentBot): \"B(a) & B(B(F) | ~d)\" and shorter \"B(a & (B(F)|~d))\" both YES. Depth-1 impossibility proof (I'll write into answer.md): any depth<=1 fully modalized phi at world n>=1 is a function of the set S of atom-triples (a,c,d) at worlds <n. At world 0 every box is true, so against FairBot the triple at world 0 is (FB vs X=□..=1, FB vs CB=□T=1, FB vs DB=□F=1) = (1,1,1), identical to CooperateBot's triple. Hence X-vs-FB at world 1 = X-vs-CB at world 1 = stable X-vs-CB = D. Then FB-vs-X = □(X vs FB) is false at all worlds >=2, so FairBot defects. Doing a brute-force min-size search for Q3 next. I will draft answer.md now; sol please review rather than overwrite.\n[sol] 2026-10-22 22:04 UTC: Smaller checked prudent formula: B(a & (d -> B(F))), depth 2, 7 syntax-tree nodes. Complete depth-1 lower bound: FB cooperation implies X(FB,n)=true for every n, hence X(FB,1)=true. At world 0 FB cooperates with X, CB, DB, so its triple is 111, identical CB. Thus X(CB,1)=true. Every depth-1 box sees the same all-111 CB history for all n>=1, so X(CB) stabilizes C, contradiction. Preparing answer.md; please review before SUBMIT.\n[sol] 2026-10-22 22:06 UTC: Race: I wrote complete answer.md just before seeing your entry asking no overwrite. Current answer uses equivalent B(a & (d -> B(F))), full verification and lower bound, size upper bound 7 (implication primitive). Please review/extend current answer rather than replace; I will not edit it further without coordination. Your size search can strengthen Q3. Core success criteria met; awaiting your review before SUBMIT.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3628ae6d-bc3f-4844-8036-102eeecb6be9","uuid":"27d3a795-affe-4a73-98b3-8b56f9843390","timestamp":"2026-10-22T22:01:26.236Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"depth 2; vs CooperateBot D, vs DefectBot D, vs FairBot C (FairBot replies C), vs itself C; prudent: YES\n  File \"/work/opus/xval.py\", line 2, in <module>\n    import check, search\nModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'search'\n[sol] 2026-10-22 22:01 UTC: Candidate depth 2: B(a) & (B(B(F)) | ~B(d)); checking now. I will prove impossibility of all depth-1 agents and seek characterization. Please independently verify candidate/proof and coordinate final answer before SUBMIT.\n[opus] 2026-10-22: Verified prudent depth-2 (PrudentBot): \"B(a) & B(B(F) | ~d)\" and shorter \"B(a & (B(F)|~d))\" both YES. Depth-1 impossibility proof (I'll write into answer.md): any depth<=1 fully modalized phi at world n>=1 is a function of the set S of atom-triples (a,c,d) at worlds <n. At world 0 every box is true, so against FairBot the triple at world 0 is (FB vs X=□..=1, FB vs CB=□T=1, FB vs DB=□F=1) = (1,1,1), identical to CooperateBot's triple. Hence X-vs-FB at world 1 = X-vs-CB at world 1 = stable X-vs-CB = D. Then FB-vs-X = □(X vs FB) is false at all worlds >=2, so FairBot defects. Doing a brute-force min-size search for Q3 next. I will draft answer.md now; sol please review rather than overwrite.\n[sol] 2026-10-22 22:04 UTC: Smaller checked prudent formula: B(a & (d -> B(F))), depth 2, 7 syntax-tree nodes. Complete depth-1 lower bound: FB cooperation implies X(FB,n)=true for every n, hence X(FB,1)=true. At world 0 FB cooperates with X, CB, DB, so its triple is 111, identical CB. Thus X(CB,1)=true. Every depth-1 box sees the same all-1