{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgJ2ey4WGKhFiHZPajFLj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012TJCGwCqrYPzYPtTLPEfwG","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /work && cat >> answer.md <<'EOF'\n\n### Size optimality (Q3, exhaustive search)\n\nWith the same node-count convention (alphabet: atoms a,c,d; constants T,F; ~; B; binary &, |, ->), the script `/work/opus/search.py` enumerates **every** syntax tree with at most 7 nodes, keeps those that are fully modalized of depth exactly 2, and evaluates them on worlds 0..19 (depth-2 sequences stabilize by world 4 or so; cross-checked against `check.py` on 3,000 random formulas from the 22,840 candidates, 0 disagreements; `/work/opus/xval.py`). Result:\n\n- sizes 1–6: no prudent formula;\n- size 7: exactly two, `B(a & (d -> B(F)))` and its commuted form `B((d -> B(F)) & a)`.\n\nHence the minimum size of a prudent depth-2 agent is **exactly 7** nodes, and up to commutativity of & the minimum-size prudent agent is unique: □(a ∧ (d → □⊥)). (Equivalent variants such as □a ∧ □(□⊥ ∨ ¬d), the classical PrudentBot \"□a ∧ □(¬□⊥ → ¬d)\", are also prudent but larger.)\nEOF\ncat >> board.md <<'EOF'\n[opus] 2026-10-22: Reviewed sol's answer.md — proofs correct, agree. Exhaustive search (/work/opus/search.py, cross-checked vs check.py): no prudent depth-2 formula with <=6 nodes; at 7 nodes exactly B(a & (d -> B(F))) and its &-commuted form. Appended \"Size optimality\" section to answer.md (no other edits). I consider answer final; sol may write SUBMIT if agreed.\n[opus] FINAL\nEOF"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1526,"cache_read_input_tokens":28008,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1526,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transforma