{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgJ2okFKQoMRfJ42fw99d","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All three questions are answered and the attempt has been submitted: sol wrote `/work/SUBMIT` after we both agreed on `/work/answer.md`.\n\n**1. Yes, a prudent agent exists, and the smallest possible depth is 2.** The agent is `FORMULA: B(a & (d -> B(F)))`, i.e. □(a ∧ (d → □⊥)). In words: cooperate if it is provable that the opponent cooperates with me and, except at world 0, defects against DefectBot. `check.py` reports it as prudent:\n\n| Opponent | Agent's move | Opponent's move |\n|---|---|---|\n| CooperateBot | D | C |\n| DefectBot | D | D |\n| FairBot | C | C |\n| Itself | C | C |\n\n**2. No agent of depth 0 or 1 is prudent, for formulas of any size.**\n- **Depth 0:** with no boxes there are no atoms, so the agent always plays the same move. It can't both defect against CooperateBot and cooperate with FairBot.\n- **Depth 1:** for FairBot to end up cooperating, the agent must cooperate with FairBot at every world, including world 1.\n  - At world 1, a depth-1 agent's move depends only on what the opponent did at world 0.\n  - At world 0, FairBot cooperates with everyone, so it looks exactly like CooperateBot. The agent therefore plays the same move against both at world 1.\n  - Against CooperateBot the depth-1 agent never changes its move after world 1. So it would end up cooperating with CooperateBot, which contradicts prudence.\n\n**3. The smallest prudent depth-2 agent has exactly 7 symbols.** Each atom, constant, connective and box counts as one symbol; parentheses don't count.\n- I enumerated every fully modalized depth-2 formula of up to 7 symbols (22,840 of them) with `/work/opus/search.py`. None of 6 symbols or fewer is prudent.\n- At 7 symbols there are exactly two prudent formulas: the one above and the same formula with the two sides of the ∧ swapped. So the smallest agent is unique up to that swap.\n- My search uses its own evaluator. It agreed with `check.py` on all 3,000 formulas in a random sample.\n- sol added a short argument that 20 worlds are always enough for these formulas to settle on their final moves.\n- Equivalent but longer versions are also prudent, such as the classical PrudentBot, □a ∧ □(¬□⊥ → ¬d).\n\nI did not attempt a full description of every prudent depth-2 agent of any size.\n\nsol wrote most of `answer.md` (the agent, the outcome table and the depth proofs). I checked it, agreed, and added the section on smallest size."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":301,"cache_read_input_tokens":31202,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":301,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":776,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3628ae6d-bc3f-4844-8036-102eeecb6be9","uuid":"ad840b40-83fd-4f9d-9ddd-1dff6a1edc44","timestamp":"2026-10-22T22:03:49.358Z","request_id":"req_011CgJ2ojL1DYkz37kmqkimQ"}
